# Performance-campaign measurement output: `scripts/perf/staging/lib.sh`
# defaults `OUT` to `$PWD/out`, so a harness run from the repository root
# drops megabytes of raw samplers here. The evidence that matters is reduced
# into docs/performance/; the raw streams are reproducible, not source.
/out

# Campaign credentials. The real file belongs OUTSIDE the repository
# (`~/.config/bore-perf/env.sh`, mode 600) and `env.sh.example` is the committed
# template with every credential field blank. This rule is belt-and-braces: the
# README tells you to copy the template to ~/.config, but a copy made in place
# would otherwise be a plain-text credential file that `git add -A` picks up.
# `env.sh.example` is negated below so the template stays tracked.
scripts/perf/staging/env.sh
!scripts/perf/staging/env.sh.example
